  "worked_solution": "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $\u0394x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\u0394y=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{\u2032}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{\u2032})\\cdot \u0394x,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{\u2032}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $\u0394y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394y & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{\u2032}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{\u2032})\\cdot \u0394x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-x+3y+(-{x}_{\\text{new}}+3{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y)+\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+\u0394y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\u0394y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y)+\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+5y)+\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(-x-{x}_{\\text{new}}+5y) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =x+{x}_{\\text{new}}-5y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
